cessible  to all of our components is before we  were creating the style sheet on import  so again no context so we deferred it to  the first render and then picked the  appropriate create method based on  directional context note we're assuming  that our apps are all wrapped in a  direction provider but again this  doesn't consider dynamically created  inline Styles so we also picked our CSS  method based on the same context and the  difference now is we pass it in as a  prop so the main change to our  components whereas previously they were  written like this we would now pull the  CSS method from our props and call it  instead this is pretty easily code  moddable I was able to write a script  that handled almost all of our cases off  the bat and the effect is pretty  stunning with just a few changes to her  like ecosystem we're about to get 95% of  the way to fully functional perfect  sight in Arabic and so we haven't yet  launched we still have a ways to go in  terms of testing across the entire  platform but we don't expect to run into  too much  the journey has already gotten this  enormous way there and we look forward  to rolling out these languages in the  future and making Airbnb a bit more  accessible to people across the world  and if you'd like to learn more highly  recommend checking out a react wa  direction package or react with Silas  package and Kent Dodds awesome our TLC  ssjspike edge and you can always tweet  at me if you have any questions thank  you  [Applause]
 

